## Environment

- Windows 11 (10.0.26100), git-bash / MSYS shell
- Node v22.23.2, backpass 0.1.3, acpx 0.13.1 (both installed via `npm i -g`)
- Harnesses present and authenticated: claude, codex, opencode, grok

## What happens

Every backpass subprocess invocation fails on Windows:

```
$ backpass
backpass v0.1.3 · backpass-trial · budget 5,000 tok · since 30d
· wrote AGENTS.md            ← bootstrap works (pure JS)
· wrote CLAUDE.md
error acpx not found on PATH (looked for "acpx")
  install acpx (npm i -g acpx) and retry
```

…even though `acpx` resolves fine in the shell (`which acpx` → `~/AppData/Roaming/npm/acpx`). After working around the acpx lookup by pinning agents, the native harness probes fail the same way, so every ladder candidate reports unavailable.

Notably everything that does **not** spawn a process works perfectly: `backpass init`, `backpass status`, `backpass scan` (all six stores fingerprinted, tier-1 association exact), distillation, prompt assembly.

## Root cause

On Windows, npm global installs expose CLIs as `.cmd` / `.ps1` shim scripts. `child_process.spawn(bin, args)` **without** `shell: true` cannot execute those shims, so every spawn dies with `spawnError ENOENT`.

There is no win32 handling in any spawn path today — `src/subprocess.js` (`runCapture`) and `src/agents.js` probes both call plain `spawn(bin, args, …)`. The only win32-aware spawn in the codebase is `src/apply/browser.js`.

## Minimal fix

One place fixes all of it, because `runCapture` is the single choke point shared by the acpx boundary and the harness probes. On win32, join the command line manually (with minimal quoting — Node's default array→string concatenation doesn't quote either) and spawn through the shell:

```js
function quoteWin32(part) {
  return /[\s"&|^<>]/.test(part) ? `"${part.replace(/"/g, '\\"')}"` : part;
}

export function runCapture(bin, args, { timeoutMs, cwd, input } = {}) {
  return new Promise((resolve) => {
    let child;
    if (process.platform === "win32") {
      const cmdline = [bin, ...args].map(quoteWin32).join(" ");
      child = spawn(cmdline, { cwd, stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "pipe"], shell: true });
    } else {
      child = spawn(bin, args, { cwd, stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "pipe"] });
    }
    // …rest unchanged…
```

I applied exactly this patch locally and the whole pipeline came alive on Windows: probes resolve, `acpx <agent> exec` runs, analysis calls are issued and transcripts get distilled.

Caveats worth a maintainer's eye:

- The quote set above covers spaces and cmd metacharacters (`& | ^ < > "`); prompts travel via `--file <path>` so long text never crosses the command line, which keeps this safe in practice.
- An alternative is resolving the real entry point (`acpx.cmd`) with `where` and spawning it directly without shell, or pulling in `cross-spawn`. The manual join has zero dependencies, which felt closer to the project's taste.

## Post-patch note (separate concern, happy to file separately)

After the spawn fix, analysis runs against a dead/unauthenticated ladder candidate surface only as `warn … analysis returned no parseable JSON`. In my case the real cause was visible only inside the harness's own store (pi session jsonl): `OpenAI API error (401): CreditsError: Insufficient balance`. It would help if `execOneShot`'s raw stdout/stderr were preserved in `.backpass/evidence/<id>.json` on failure — the evidence files currently record just `"status": "failed"` plus a generic message. Fail-loud behavior itself worked great (no silent fallthrough), this is purely about making the loud failure diagnosable.

## Intent

REBASE/CONFLICT RECOVERY (not a re-implementation): the cluster domain-voting improvement (backpass #5) is COMPLETE and was green on PR #86 (branch fm/backpass-cluster-domain-vote-r1, head b4872829250c14dfa8d78fcf24eb4c557df5d417), but a sibling backpass PR (#85, corpus classification) landed first, so #86 now has merge conflicts with main and cannot merge.

Reconcile and re-land that work; do NOT redesign or re-implement the feature. The existing #86 work is authoritative. This branch (fm/backpass-cluster-vote-rebase-recovery-r1) was created from that head and rebased onto current origin/main. Resolve conflicts by PRESERVING BOTH SIDES: keep #86's domain-voting / report-only-accounting / status-counting changes AND every change already on main from #85 and other landed backpass PRs. Do NOT drop, revert, or overwrite either side's logic. Conflicts were expected where both touched src/fold.js, src/gap-ledger.js, src/proposal.js, src/commands/propose.js, and tests; merge the intents, do not pick one.

This is purely a rebase + conflict reconciliation + re-validation of already-completed, already-reviewed work. After resolving, the test suite must stay green, the rebased branch must be pushed, and no-mistakes must go GREEN on the new head so it can land under the project's yolo-on posture.

## What Changed

- Cluster all gap sightings before applying per-session project or orchestration domain votes, with ties remaining synthesis eligible and majority-orchestration clusters excluded.
- Keep mixed and corroborated excluded clusters visible as report-only evidence while preventing them from reaching synthesis.
- Update status, progress counts, proposal statistics, and the apply funnel to distinguish synthesis-eligible, report-only, and below-threshold clusters.

## Risk Assessment

✅ Low: The target is based on current main, preserves the authoritative feature source, and introduces no substantiated correctness or intent-conformance issues.

## Testing

Inspected the rebased change, ran targeted fold, ledger, CLI, proposal, bootstrap, and status tests, then manually verified domain voting through generated report and synthesis outputs and the rendered apply UI. Tied mixed-domain clusters remained synthesis eligible, majority-orchestration clusters were report only, below-floor singletons stayed hidden, and the worktree remained clean.

- Evidence: [Rendered apply UI showing post-clustering gap funnel and report-only count](https://github.com/kunchenguid/backpass/blob/5a0d8c0ad1b1af8dd231c5854af67c411efc1839/.no-mistakes/evidence/fm/backpass-cluster-vote-rebase-recovery-r1/apply-domain-vote.png)

