Backpass 0.1.26 does not redact unassigned credentials that use the common `apikey_<token>` shape.

Minimal reproduction:

```js
import { redact } from "./src/redact.js";

const fake = `apikey_${"a".repeat(64)}`;
console.log(redact(fake) === fake);
```

This prints `true`. If that shape appears in a user message rather than a `KEY=value` assignment, the full value is retained in the distilled analysis prompt and can be sent to the configured model.

Expected: replace the full value with a redaction label, with a regression test for both lowercase `apikey_` and uppercase variants.

Observed locally: the unredacted value was also retained in the generated prompt cache. The affected cache entry was removed without changing the source transcript.

## Intent

Make annotate evidence trustworthy and reviewable: analysis should locate each accepted quote in the distilled trace, fold should carry that locator window onto catalog quotes, the proposal gate should require every annotate evidence quote to uniquely match a fold-issued catalog quote from the same source (refusing invented or ambiguous quotes), and the apply surfaces should show the before/after context span when a locator exists.

## What Changed

- Analysis now finds each accepted evidence quote in the distilled trace (`locateQuote` in `src/analyze.js`). It records a locator (folded offset, plus turn and role when a turn heading comes before the quote) and keeps up to 120 characters of trace on each side. Fold (`src/fold.js`) and the gap ledger (`src/gap-ledger.js`) copy the locator and the before/after text onto catalog quotes, so gap clusters built from the ledger show the same context as clusters built in the same run.
- When fold has issued source labels, `buildProposal` (`src/proposal.js`) checks every annotate evidence quote against the fold catalog. Each quote must exactly match a catalog quote from the same source, or be a substring of one at least 8 characters long; a trailing ellipsis copied from a truncated render is ignored. Quotes with invented text, or that match more than one catalog quote, are refused, and only quotes that pass count toward the session-evidence floor. Matching gap IDs and counting evidence projects now use the same normalized lookup. The annotate prompt, README, and AGENTS.md describe the new rule.
- The terminal apply view and the HTML review page (`templates/apply.html`) show the trace text before and after a quote when a locator exists: dimmed lines in the terminal, and a click-to-expand section on the HTML page. Quotes without a locator display as before and are not refused.

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)

## Risk Assessment

✅ Low: The round-1 fix (R1) correctly narrows matchingCatalogQuotes to exact folded hits when any exist, and because the shared helper is reused, the gate, uniqueMatchingGapIds and countedEvidenceProjects all get the same behavior. Polarity collapsing and the ellipsis stripping still work as the recorded decisions require, and the new regression test asserts the correct binding (negative/harm row, 2 transcripts).

## Testing

I rebuilt a disposable end-to-end setup: an isolated HOME with three real Claude-format sessions, a git repo, and a stand-in acpx. Through it I drove the real backpass CLI across analyze, propose and both apply surfaces, as the terminal (in a sized pty) and as the HTML surface (rendered and screenshotted in headless Chrome). Analysis attached a locator and window to every quote. Gap-cluster quotes built from the ledger now keep that window through gap-ledger.json and proposal.json, and both apply surfaces show the before/after context with the quote printed once; this was the round-1 failure. The annotate gate refused invented, wrong-source, too-short and ambiguous quotes with clear violations and exit 1. It accepted exact, trailing-ellipsis and substring citations, widening substring context to the full catalog quote, and bound an exact quote to its own row rather than a containing one. The focused gap-ledger and fold tests also pass. Temp setup was removed and only evidence files remain.

