- ⚠️ `src/proposal.js:206` - matchingCatalogQuotes counts any catalog quote that contains the cited text, so an exact match never beats a containing match. Example: session S has catalog quote X &#34;pnpm check failed&#34; (say an instruction negative) and a gap quote Y &#34;ran pnpm check failed twice, then committed&#34;. If the model cites X verbatim, it matches X exactly and Y as a substring, so the edit is refused with &#34;cite a longer unique span&#34;. No longer span of X exists, so X can never be cited on its own. Citing Y instead binds the evidence to Y&#39;s row, which can attach the edit to the wrong gap in uniqueMatchingGapIds (line 436) and countedEvidenceProjects (line 465), or drop that session below minGapEvidence. Analysis quoting overlapping spans from one session for a negative and a gap is a normal pattern. Fix: when one or more candidates&#39; folded text equals citedText(item.text), restrict the matches to those exact hits before applying the uniqueness check. The other callers of matchingCatalogQuotes (lines 436 and 469) get the same fix through the shared helper.

🔧 Fix applied.
