- ⚠️ `src/analyze.js:554` - In analyzePending, outcome is set to &#34;ok&#34; right after a successful analyzeOne call, but the subsequent state.writeEvidence(...) call in the same try block can still throw (e.g. ENOSPC/EACCES writing the evidence JSON, per writeJsonFile in src/state.js:154-156). If it does, the catch block unconditionally reassigns outcome = err.modelCallAttempted ? &#34;failed-attempted&#34; : &#34;failed&#34;. Since this err originates after analyzeOne already returned successfully, err.modelCallAttempted is undefined, so outcome becomes &#34;failed&#34; even though the model call fully succeeded. For the warm-up loop, called stays false (outcome === &#34;ok&#34; || outcome === &#34;failed-attempted&#34; is false), so a transcript whose Claude call actually completed (which would have let a due OAuth refresh finish) is not recognized as having called the model, and the serial warm-up wrongly continues to another transcript instead of proceeding to the fan-out. This does not reproduce the #203 race itself (the loop stays serial either way), but it breaks the &#39;called&#39; invariant the fix depends on: a completed model call must count as called. The smallest fix is to stop the catch block from overwriting an outcome already set to &#34;ok&#34; (or to scope the catch so only an analyzeOne failure can change outcome), not to add new retry or degradation machinery.

🔧 Fix applied.
